{
  "note": [
    "A SNAPSHOT OF THE LIVE CHAIN BEFORE THE \"EMERGENCY BRAKE\" CUT (3 September 2026).",
    "Read off Base Sepolia at block 46306403 with the public endpoint, NOT derived from",
    "any script's own lists and NOT copied out of a document. CLAUDE.md forbids the",
    "second: addresses and selector counts come from the chain or from",
    "broadcast/<Script>.s.sol/84532/run-latest.json, never from prose.",
    "",
    "WHY IT IS HERE. The stand of a cut has to answer \"which group does each selector go",
    "in\" -- Replace reverts on an unmounted selector, Add reverts on a mounted one, and",
    "either mistake drops the WHOLE cut in one transaction after three facets have been",
    "paid for. A stand that answered that question out of the script's own",
    "replaceSelectors() would agree with itself no matter how the groups were filed.",
    "That is the fourth way to be fooled by a measurement, and on 16 August it cost a",
    "whole cut: the sabotage turned two neighbours red and left the appointed lock",
    "green. The expected side lives here, in data read from the chain.",
    "",
    "THE THREE FACETS WERE IDENTIFIED BY SET EQUALITY AGAINST THE BUILD ARTIFACTS, not",
    "by their selector counts: JobBoardFacet and ServiceBoardFacet match their compiled",
    "ABIs exactly (13 and 25), and FactoryFacet matches on all 23 it routes while the",
    "compiled facet stands FIVE ahead -- those five being this cut's Add group.",
    "",
    "THE ADD GROUP IS TWO DELIVERIES, AND THEY ARE RECORDED SEPARATELY BELOW. Four are",
    "the emergency brake (decision 17), in `brakeSelectors`. The fifth is `MAX_FEE_BPS()`",
    "= 0xd55be8c6 (item 138), in `feeCapSelectors` -- the 20% fee ceiling that stood as a",
    "bare `2_000` in `initFeeModel` and `setFeeBps` and could be read from nowhere. They",
    "are kept in two lists rather than one because they are two decisions that happen to",
    "ride in one transaction; a single widened list would let one absorb a drift belonging",
    "to the other. Both were read the same way and both answer facetAddress() with the",
    "zero address: `cast call $DIAMOND \"facetAddress(bytes4)(address)\" 0xd55be8c6",
    "--rpc-url https://sepolia.base.org` returns 0x0000...0000."
  ],
